      "message": "feat(motion): the rotary wrap turns its seam clear of a D-flat instead of refusing it\n\nThe wrap refused by name any work whose default seam (the basis' +-pi\nbranch) crossed a feature that is not turned, so a D-flat bar wrapped only\nin some placements. Now, when the default seam is refused, the wrap\nsearches the azimuths midway between vertex columns for a seam where every\nstraddling facet stands on two alike meridian columns\n(multiaxis::rotary_seam_angle), takes the middle of the widest turned\nband, turns the azimuth basis there and lays the development out again\n(multiaxis::rotary_sheet, the lap loop moved out of rotary_offset). The\nturned sheet is re-judged by the same seam law, and the world exit maps\nback through the same basis, so only the split moves - every point is cut\nat its true azimuth. A seam that is already turned is kept, so every\nexisting wrap is byte-identical. A feature all the way round is still\nrefused by name.\n\nPinned by rotary_dflat::{an_off_centre_flat_across_the_seam_never_puts_a_tip_in_the_part\n(all 36 placements wrap, 0 tips inside), a_d_flat_bar_wraps_in_every_placement\n(channel tips at the flat's true azimuth),\na_flat_channel_across_the_default_seam_develops_under_adaptive_and_rings,\na_feature_all_the_way_round_is_still_refused_by_name}.\n\nFixes #226\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
